24:["$","p",null,{"style":{"color":"var(--text-secondary)","marginBottom":"1.5rem","lineHeight":1.7},"children":"The system utilizes an API Gateway routing traffic to three distinct Spring Boot services: Auth Service (JWT issuance), Account Service (balance management with pessimistic locking), and Transaction Ledger Service (immutable audit trail). Database transactions execute at `SERIALIZABLE` or `READ_COMMITTED` with row-level locking on balance modifications."}]
2e:T693,+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                         CLIENT / WEB DASHBOARD                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                     |
                                     | (HTTPS / Bearer Token)
                                     v
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                         API GATEWAY & SECURITY                          |
|           (Spring Cloud Gateway / Spring Security JWT Filter)           |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                 |                                         |
                 v                                         v
+----------------------------------+     +----------------------------------+
|        ACCOUNT SERVICE           |     |     TRANSACTION AUDIT LEDGER     |
| (Spring Boot 3 / Hibernate JPA)  |     |  (Append-Only Financial Records) |
+----------------------------------+     +----------------------------------+
                 |                                         |
                 v                                         v
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                        POSTGRESQL REPOSITORY                            |
|  - Accounts Table (Row-Level Pessimistic Locking: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE)|
|  - Ledger Transactions (Immutable Double-Entry Bookkeeping)             |
|  - Idempotency Keys Cache Table (24-Hour Expiry Window)                 |
